1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:03,320
Erm... hello Professor, I'm John Wishart

2
00:00:04,060 --> 00:00:05,463
I'm working on my entry for the Global Design Competition.

3
00:00:05,463 --> 00:00:09,560
My tutor said you might be able to help me with it.

4
00:00:09,560 --> 00:00:12,320
Ah, yes, I got a copy of your drawings

5
00:00:12,800 --> 00:00:15,710
Come in and tell me about it. What sort of competition is it?

6
00:00:15,710 --> 00:00:17,865
Well, it's an international design competition

7
00:00:17,865 --> 00:00:23,610
and we have to come up with a new design for a typical domestic kitchen appliance.

8
00:00:23,610 --> 00:00:26,580
I see, and are there any special conditions

9
00:00:26,860 --> 00:00:29,020
Does it have to save energy for example?

10
00:00:29,020 --> 00:00:33,630
Actually that was the focus in last year's competition. This year's different.

11
00:00:33,630 --> 00:00:36,911
We have to adopt an innovative approach to existing technology,

12
00:00:36,911 --> 00:00:40,520
using it in a way that hasn't been thought of before.

13
00:00:40,520 --> 00:00:45,040
I see, that sounds tricky. And what kitchen appliance have you chosen?

14
00:00:45,040 --> 00:00:47,920
Well, I decided to choose the dishwasher.

15
00:00:47,920 --> 00:00:50,900
Interesting, what made you choose that?

16
00:00:50,900 --> 00:00:54,576
Well, they're an everyday kitchen appliance in most Australian houses

17
00:00:54,576 --> 00:00:58,620
but they're all pretty boring and almost identical to each other.

18
00:00:58,620 --> 00:01:03,640
I think some people will be prepared to pay a little extra for something that looks different.

19
00:01:03,640 --> 00:01:09,500
That's a nice idea. I see you've called your design 'the Rockpool'; why is that?

20
00:01:09,500 --> 00:01:13,260
Basically because it looks like the rock pools you find on a beach.

21
00:01:13,260 --> 00:01:17,310
The top is made of glass so that you can look down into it.

22
00:01:17,310 --> 00:01:20,860
And there's a stone at the bottom. Is that just for decoration?

23
00:01:20,860 --> 00:01:26,250
Actually it does have a function. Instead of pushing a button, you turn the stone.

24
00:01:26,250 --> 00:01:30,210
So it's really just a novel way of starting the dishwasher.

25
00:01:30,210 --> 00:01:31,100
That's right.

26
00:01:31,100 --> 00:01:35,020
It's a really nice design, but what makes it innovative?

27
00:01:35,020 --> 00:01:39,910
Well, I decided to make a dishwasher that uses carbon dioxide.

28
00:01:39,910 --> 00:01:43,490
In place of water and detergent? How will you manage that?

29
00:01:43,490 --> 00:01:48,096
The idea is to pressurise the carbon dioxide so that it becomes a liquid.

30
00:01:48,096 --> 00:01:51,060
The fluid is then released into the dishwasher

31
00:01:51,060 --> 00:01:53,360
where it cleans the dishes all by itself.

32
00:01:53,360 --> 00:01:55,600
Sounds like a brilliant idea

33
00:01:56,080 --> 00:01:59,813
Your system will totally do away with the need for strong detergents.

34
00:01:59,813 --> 00:02:02,850
So what happens once the dishes are clean?

35
00:02:02,850 --> 00:02:04,927
Well, to allow them to dry,

36
00:02:04,927 --> 00:02:10,810
the liquid carbon dioxide and the waste materials all go to an area called the holding chamber.

37
00:02:10,810 --> 00:02:14,753
That's where the liquid is depressurised and so it reverts to a gas.

38
00:02:14,753 --> 00:02:19,000
Then the oil and grease are separated out and sent to the waste system.

39
00:02:19,000 --> 00:02:22,250
It sounds like you've thought it all out very thoroughly.

40
00:02:22,250 --> 00:02:28,260
So, what happens to the carbon dioxide once the process is complete? Not wasted I hope.

41
00:02:28,260 --> 00:02:30,920
Actually, that's where the real savings are made.

42
00:02:30,920 --> 00:02:36,620
The carbon dioxide is sent back to the cylinder and can be used again and again.

43
00:02:36,620 --> 00:02:40,400
What a terrific idea. Do you think it will ever be built?

44
00:02:40,400 --> 00:02:42,760
Probably not, but that's OK.

45
00:02:42,760 --> 00:02:47,540
Well, I'm sure a lot of positive things will come out of your design.

46
00:02:47,540 --> 00:02:50,640
Now, you seem to have thought about everything

47
00:02:50,700 --> 00:02:53,210
so what exactly did you need me to help you with?

48
00:02:53,210 --> 00:02:58,756
Well, my design has made it to the final stage of the competition and, in a few months' time.

49
00:02:58,756 --> 00:03:01,260
I have to give a presentation

50
00:03:01,260 --> 00:03:04,010
and that's the part I was hoping you could help me with.

51
00:03:04,010 --> 00:03:08,560
Right, well that should be easy enough. What have you managed to do so far?

52
00:03:08,560 --> 00:03:12,180
Well, I've got detailed drawings to show how it will work

53
00:03:12,180 --> 00:03:14,700
and I've also written a 500-word paper on it.

54
00:03:14,700 --> 00:03:20,250
I see. Well, if you want to stand a good chance of winning you really need a model of the machine.

55
00:03:20,250 --> 00:03:23,440
Yes, I thought I might but I'm having a few problems.

56
00:03:23,440 --> 00:03:28,230
What is the main difficulty so far? Let me guess - is it the materials?

57
00:03:28,230 --> 00:03:31,000
Yes. I want it to look professional

58
00:03:31,000 --> 00:03:34,290
but everything that's top quality is also very expensive.

59
00:03:34,290 --> 00:03:37,520
Look, projects like this are very important to us

60
00:03:37,560 --> 00:03:39,660
They really help lift our profile.

61
00:03:39,660 --> 00:03:42,573
So why don't you talk to the university about a grant?

62
00:03:42,573 --> 00:03:45,750
I can help you fill out the application forms if you like.

63
00:03:45,750 --> 00:03:47,070
That would be great.

64
00:03:47,070 --> 00:03:50,167
You'd better show me this paper you've written as well.

65
00:03:50,167 --> 00:03:52,300
For a global competition such as this

66
00:03:52,740 --> 00:03:56,670
you need to make sure the technical details you've given are accurate and thorough.

67
00:03:56,670 --> 00:03:58,150
That would be a great help.

68
00:03:58,150 --> 00:04:00,040
Is there anything else I can do?

69
00:04:00,040 --> 00:04:01,510
Well, I'm really....
